problem:
Problem description
- There is a single-period procurement planning problem with a finite supplier set $$\mathcal{S}$$ containing the designated suppliers $$A$$, $$B$$, and $$C$$.
- Each supplier $$i \in \mathcal{S}$$ has an order cost parameter $$c_i$$ and a fixed lot-size parameter $$q_i$$, meaning one order from supplier $$i$$ provides exactly $$q_i$$ tables.
- The restaurant chooses a nonnegative integer number of orders from each supplier, and may use supplier-activation indicators to express conditional purchasing rules.
- The total number of tables obtained from all suppliers must be at least the minimum required demand level $$D^{\min}$$ and must not exceed the maximum allowed supply level $$D^{\max}$$.
- If supplier $$A$$ is used, then supplier $$B$$ must provide at least the required minimum quantity $$L_{A \rightarrow B}$$ of tables.
- If supplier $$B$$ is used, then supplier $$C$$ must also be used.
- The planning goal is to minimize the total procurement cost across all suppliers.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_i$$: the nonnegative integer number of orders placed with supplier $$i \in \mathcal{S}$$.
  - $$z_i$$: a binary indicator showing whether supplier $$i$$ is used.
  - $$t_i$$: the total number of tables procured from supplier $$i$$.
  - $$T$$: the total number of tables ordered across all suppliers.
  - $$Z$$: the minimum total procurement cost achieved by the plan.

Input Format
{
  "supplier_set": {
    "name": "$$\\mathcal{S}$$",
    "size": "$$S$$",
    "elements": "A finite set of suppliers indexed by $$i \\in \\mathcal{S}$$"
  },
  "supplier_parameters": [
    {
      "id": "$$i$$",
      "cost_per_order": "$$c_i$$",
      "tables_per_order": "$$q_i$$"
    }
  ],
  "planning_horizon": {
    "period_set": "$$\\mathcal{H}$$",
    "size": "$$H$$",
    "description": "The ordering horizon, which may be a single period or multiple periods"
  },
  "demand_limits": {
    "minimum_total_tables": "$$D^{\\min}$$",
    "maximum_total_tables": "$$D^{\\max}$$"
  },
  "logical_rules": [
    {
      "type": "quantity_dependency",
      "trigger_supplier": "$$i$$",
      "required_supplier": "$$j$$",
      "minimum_quantity_if_trigger_used": "$$L_{ij}$$"
    },
    {
      "type": "usage_dependency",
      "trigger_supplier": "$$i$$",
      "required_supplier": "$$j$$"
    }
  ],
  "variable_domains": {
    "order_counts": "Nonnegative integer-valued for all $$i \\in \\mathcal{S}$$",
    "supplier_usage": "Binary for all $$i \\in \\mathcal{S}$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "orders_by_supplier": {
    "shape": "$$S$$",
    "symbol": "$$\\mathbf{x} = (x_i)_{i \\in \\mathcal{S}}$$",
    "description": "The integer number of orders placed with each supplier"
  },
  "supplier_usage": {
    "shape": "$$S$$",
    "symbol": "$$\\mathbf{z} = (z_i)_{i \\in \\mathcal{S}}$$",
    "description": "The binary supplier-activation vector"
  },
  "tables_by_supplier": {
    "shape": "$$S$$",
    "symbol": "$$\\mathbf{t} = (t_i)_{i \\in \\mathcal{S}}$$",
    "description": "The total number of tables procured from each supplier"
  },
  "total_tables": {
    "shape": "$$1$$",
    "symbol": "$$T$$",
    "description": "The total number of tables ordered across all suppliers"
  },
  "total_cost": {
    "shape": "$$1$$",
    "symbol": "$$Z$$",
    "description": "The minimum total procurement cost"
  }
}

Example(s)

